'''''Passiflora antioquiensis''''', the '''red banana passionfruit''', is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Passifloraceae]].<ref name=POWO>{{cite web |url= https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:674787-1 |title= Passiflora antioquiensis H.Karst. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=n.d. |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=The Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=February 4, 2025}}</ref><ref name=COL>{{cite web |url= https://www.catalogueoflife.org/data/taxon/75SDD |title= Passiflora antioquiensis H.Karst. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=n.d. |website=Catalogue of Life |publisher=Species 2000 |access-date=February 4, 2025}}</ref> It is native to [[Colombia]] and is named for the [[Antioquia Department]] in Colombia where the [[biological type|type specimen]] was collected. It was originally described by [[Gustav Karl Wilhelm Hermann Karsten]] in 1859.<ref name="Passiflora">Ulmer, T., and J.M. MacDougal. 2004. ''[https://books.google.com/books?id=43bVC3P8PJsC&pg=PA335 ''Passiflora'': Passionflowers of the World.]'' Portland, Oregon: Timber Press. p. 335.</ref> It has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref>{{cite web |title=''Passiflora antioquiensis'' H. Karst. banana passion fruit |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/119921/Neoporteria-paucicostata/Details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=16 June 2021 }}</ref> With ''[[Passiflora tripartita]]'' var. ''mollissima'' it was hybridised in the [[Veitch Nurseries]] in Exeter, England in the 1870s to yield ''[[Passiflora × exoniensis]]'', which has also gained the Award of Garden Merit.<ref>{{cite web 
|url=http://www.roselandhouse.co.uk/climbers/passiflora%20exoniensis.htm
|title=Passiflora x exoniensis |publisher=Roseland.co.uk |access-date=18 April 2018 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Passiflora antioquiensis'' H. Karst. banana passion fruit |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/72478/Passiflora-antioquiensis-H-Karst/Details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=16 June 2021 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Passiflora'' × ''exoniensis'' Exeter passion flower |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/76115/Passiflora-x-exoniensis/Details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=16 June 2021 }}</ref>

